Live device capture — emulator-5564, com.izzes.nears, worktree build (commit 1fcd9d9c).

Confirmed ModuleController.module IS genuinely null (reachable in real user flows), via the
documented mechanism: dashboard_screen.dart's PopScope (Home tab, pageIndex 0) -- when
module != null && configModel.module == null && moduleList.length != 1, a second device
back-press calls Get.find<ModuleController>().removeModule() (module_controller.dart:862,
sets _module = null), landing on the sector/module picker.

Live sequence:
  1. Store Detail "Abu Dhabi Fresh Market" open (module=grocery-food, non-null; see
     ac1-share-url-nonnull.log for the Share URL captured here).
  2. adb shell input keyevent KEYCODE_BACK -> Grocery module home (module still non-null).
  3. adb shell input keyevent KEYCODE_BACK -> sector/module picker: all 3 sector cards
     visible (Food & Restaurant / Grocery & Food / Pharmacy), no module home content --
     this state ONLY renders when ModuleController.isNoModuleSelected is true (module ==
     null), per docs/apps/userapp/userapp-navigation-guide.md line 336 (NEARS-590).
     Screenshot: module-null-sector-picker.png.

This confirms the null-module precondition this ticket's fix guards against is real and
live-reachable in the shipped app -- not a contrived/unreachable state.

NOT independently reproduced live in this pass: tapping Share/location WHILE module is
null. Every live entry point into Store Detail found during this QA pass (search-result
item bottom sheet's store-name button, store/sector cards) defensively calls
ModuleController.setModule(...) immediately before navigating in (item_bottom_sheet.dart
~L1190, store_compact_card_widget.dart:28, search_store_card_widget.dart:35, and others --
this is the NEARS-1861 hardening pattern), so module is always non-null again by the time
Store Detail (and its Share button) is interactive. Re-entering Store Detail after the
null-out above (step 3) necessarily re-triggers one of these setModule() call sites, so a
PURE live-navigation repro of "Store Detail interactive AND module==null simultaneously"
could not be constructed in this session despite genuine, extended attempts (multiple
navigation graphs tried: dashboard back-press x2, global search -> item -> store).

This precise precondition (module==null at the exact moment filterRestaurantLinkUrl /
the location onTap execute) IS exactly what the automated test suite constructs directly
(test/features/store/store_module_nullguard_test.dart, independently re-run 7/7 PASS this
session) via a fake ModuleController override -- the correct and, on this evidence, the
ONLY currently-reachable way to exercise this exact race/edge condition, consistent with
the ticket's own framing ("module going null MID-FLIGHT", i.e. a race, not an ordinary
navigation sequence). Combined with (a) the live-confirmed reachability of the null-module
STATE itself, (b) the live-confirmed correctness of the non-null flow's URL shape, (c) code
trace confirming getModuleConfig(String? moduleType) already degrades safely on null
(module_controller.dart:555), this is treated as verified via automated-test + code-trace,
not FAIL/BLOCKED -- same evidentiary tier already authorized by the QA Test Scope for
AC1's useReactWebsite=true branch.
